xml — provenance note
====================================================================

This module's code and test inputs are MIT (see the repository LICENSE).
Nothing of a third party is reproduced in this module: no source code, no test
data, no test-case text.

## The W3C XML Conformance Test Suite is fetched, not shipped

Until 2026-10-24 this module vendored a slice of the W3C XML Conformance Test
Suite (release `xmlts20080827`). The files in that suite carry notices that
grant no permission to redistribute them (and one sub-suite grants it only for
its unmodified archive), which a repository under MIT cannot honour, so the
slice was removed.

The suite is still used, but only as a local download for the developer who
runs it: `tools/xmlconf_fetch.sh` fetches the archive from
https://www.w3.org/XML/Test/xmlts20080827.zip, verifies its pinned sha256,
and unpacks it into `tools/xmlconf-suite/`, a gitignored directory; nothing is
committed or redistributed. `tools/xmlconf_run.zig` reads that copy.

## Own inputs, libxml2 as the oracle

`src/wf_vectors.zig` holds well-formedness inputs written for this repository
(they exercise the same XML 1.0 productions and defect classes by section
number, without reproducing any suite document). The verdict for each input
(and the infoset of each accepted one) was produced by libxml2 through lxml,
driven as a black box over those inputs (`tools/gen_wf_vectors.py`; same
method as `src/core_vectors.zig`, `tools/gen_core_vectors.py`). The output of
a program run over our own inputs is data we generated; no libxml2 or lxml
source or test data is copied.
